-- ============================================================================
-- DC18 - Seismolord PROFESSIONAL (intermediate tier) goes deep.
--
-- Flips (seismolord, intermediate) onto the DC1 deep path by inserting
-- its ACTIVE academy_course_structures row, generated from the repo
-- manifest src/content/courses/seismolord/intermediate/manifest.json
-- (the structure source of truth; emitted by a generator, not
-- hand-typed), and seeding the module quiz banks plus the final exam.
-- Answer keys live only here and in the table.
--
-- Every numeric item traces to the seismolord teaching oracle and
-- reproduces the live NG6 Professional capstone answer key: the bulk
-- shift scan over a synthetic arriving 8 ms late (shift 8 ms,
-- correlation exactly 1 because the exercise is an autocorrelation),
-- and the wavelet-frequency pair (strongest amplitude 0.1573149710893631
-- at 1580 ms for 15 Hz, 0.0362229160964489 at 1646 ms for 40 Hz). Same
-- pipeline src/lib/seismolordTeaching.js drives and shiftLab.test.js
-- pins.
--
-- Tier note: the Associate tier (DC7) BUILT the synthetic and already
-- teaches the 15/25/40 amplitude and time table. This tier deliberately
-- does not re-teach it: the banks test the mechanism and the
-- professional consequence (scan rather than eyeball, a pick carries its
-- wavelet, amplitudes are not comparable across surveys) rather than
-- recall of the tier below. The Expert tier owns wedge tuning and AVO.
--
-- Bank standard: measured on the length RANK of the correct option and
-- checked for cyclic key sequences before seeding, per DC12.
--
-- Enrollment grandfathering: enforced_from defaults to now() on first
-- insert, so learners enrolled before this apply finish on the old path;
-- the ON CONFLICT update deliberately leaves enforced_from unchanged on
-- re-seeds. Re-seeding replaces the whole bank for this course-tier;
-- fine while there are no open attempts (open attempts pin question ids).
-- ============================================================================

values ('seismolord', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-from-tie-to-shift","title":"From Tie to Shift","lesson_keys":["l01-what-this-tier-adds","l02-the-planted-lag","l03-what-a-bulk-shift-is","l04-the-shift-panel-map"]},{"key":"m02-the-correlation-scan","title":"The Correlation Scan","lesson_keys":["l01-comparing-two-traces","l02-the-normalised-correlation","l03-scanning-the-lags","l04-reading-the-peak","l05-why-a-correlation-of-one-is-a-synthetic-answer"]},{"key":"m03-reading-the-scan-curve","title":"Reading the Scan Curve","lesson_keys":["l01-the-shape-of-the-curve","l02-zero-lag-is-not-innocent","l03-how-sharp-is-the-peak","l04-when-the-scan-misleads"]},{"key":"m04-tuning-moves-the-amplitude","title":"Tuning Moves the Amplitude","lesson_keys":["l01-the-wavelet-sets-the-amplitude","l02-lower-frequency-larger-peak","l03-why-that-is-backwards","l04-amplitude-is-not-reflectivity"]},{"key":"m05-tuning-moves-the-time","title":"Tuning Moves the Time","lesson_keys":["l01-the-peak-time-is-not-fixed","l02-the-reflectivity-never-moves","l03-sixty-six-milliseconds","l04-which-time-do-you-pick","l05-what-this-costs-a-tie"]},{"key":"m06-the-shift-workflow","title":"The Shift Workflow","lesson_keys":["l01-the-workflow-end-to-end","l02-quality-control","l03-the-capstone-walkthrough","l04-onward-to-expert"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

